<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to April 16 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.37 (0.37)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.47 (0.48)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.91 (0.93)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.32 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.42 (0.43)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.86 (0.88)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.27 (0.28)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.37 (0.38)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  0.81 (0.83)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Apr 14 - Apr 18:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.52 (0.53)   120-150 days  0.60 (0.57)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.54 (0.56)   150-180 days  0.57 (0.59)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.54 (0.55)   180-360 days  0.65 (0.58)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.55 (0.55)   over 360 days 0.70 (0.61)</p>
</text>
